Hydra
=====

A reverse proxy that exposes Google Antigravity (Gemini) models through
OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible APIs.  Bind multiple Google accounts,
let Hydra handle OAuth refresh and quota-aware load balancing, then
point any OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible client at it.

Hydra 是一个反向代理，把 Google Antigravity (Gemini) 模型通过 OpenAI 和
Anthropic 兼容 API 暴露出来。绑定多个 Google 账号，让 Hydra 处理 OAuth
刷新和配额感知的负载均衡，然后把任何 OpenAI/Anthropic 兼容客户端指向它。


Features
--------

  * OpenAI API: /v1/chat/completions, /v1/models, /responses
  * Anthropic API: /v1/messages, /v1/messages/count_tokens
  * Multi-account pooling with three scheduling modes:
    cache, balance, performance
  * Quota protection: auto-disables models at quota threshold,
    re-enables on recovery
  * API key management with per-key usage tracking,
    rotate / enable / disable
  * TUI dashboard: inspect accounts, logs, models, keys, and usage
    in the terminal
  * SQLite request logging with token breakdown
  * Prometheus metrics at /metrics
  * JSON mode, image and audio input via OpenAI content parts


Install
-------

Homebrew (macOS):

    brew tap deungjaho/hydra
    brew install hydra

AUR (Arch Linux):

    yay -S hydra-proxy

From source / 从源码编译:

    make build
    # or: go build ./cmd/hydra


Quick start
-----------

  1. Bind a Google account (starts OAuth flow):

       hydra accounts add

  2. Start the proxy (auto-creates a default API key on first run):

       hydra serve

  3. Point a client at it:

       curl http://127.0.0.1:18045/v1/chat/completions \
         -H "Authorization: Bearer <your-api-key>" \
         -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
         -d '{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash-high","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}]}'

  4. Open the TUI dashboard:

       hydra


Commands
--------

    hydra                      TUI dashboard
    hydra serve                start the proxy server
    hydra accounts add         bind a Google account via OAuth
    hydra accounts list        list bound accounts
    hydra key add <label>      create a new API key
    hydra key list             list API keys and usage
    hydra key rotate <id>      rotate an API key (old key invalidated)
    hydra key show <id>        print the full key string
    hydra quota                refresh quota from Google API
    hydra usage [-w day|week|month|all]
                               show usage statistics
    hydra logs                 show recent request logs
    hydra config               show or reset configuration
    hydra version              print version


Configuration
-------------

Config file: ~/.config/hydra/config.toml

Environment variables override config file values:

    HYDRA_PORT                 proxy.port                  default 18045
    HYDRA_BIND                 proxy.bind                  default 127.0.0.1
    HYDRA_UPSTREAM_PROXY       proxy.upstream_proxy        default none
    HYDRA_LOG_REQUESTS         proxy.log_requests          default true
    HYDRA_SCHEDULING_MODE      scheduling.mode             default balance
    HYDRA_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID      --                          default Antigravity's
    HYDRA_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET  --                          default Antigravity's

Scheduling modes / 调度模式:

    cache        each session sticks to one account (maximize cache hits)
    balance      sticky + switch on quota/degradation
    performance  power-of-two-choices random sampling

See config.example.toml for a full example.


TUI keybindings
---------------

    Tab / 1-5    switch tab
    j / k        navigate up/down
    Ctrl+d/u     scroll (Logs tab)
    Space        expand log detail (Logs tab)
    a            add key (Keys tab)
    K            rotate key (Keys tab)
    s            show full key (Keys tab)
    D            delete row
    e            enable/disable
    r            refresh quota
    w            switch time window (Status tab)
    m            switch scheduling mode (Status tab)
    q            quit


OAuth credentials
-----------------

Hydra reuses the Antigravity desktop app's Google OAuth client ID and
secret.  OAuth desktop clients are "public" client types where the
secret is embedded in the client binary and is not truly confidential.

If Google revokes the default client ID, point Hydra at your own
Google OAuth desktop client via HYDRA_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and
HYDRA_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET.


Development
-----------

    make build       build to bin/hydra
    make test        go test -count=1 ./...
    make vet         go vet ./...
    make fmt         gofmt + goimports
    make fmt-check   CI format check

